<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p>
This engineering progress report presents the cumulative accomplishments, technical audit findings, architectural integration, and automated verification milestones achieved across <strong>Phases 1 through 8</strong> for the <strong>MSU-Naawan Automated Payroll Management System</strong>.
</p>
<p>
The primary objective was to transition a fragmented prototype and disconnected database baseline into a fully integrated, verified, and testable institutional payroll platform adhering to Philippine Civil Service Commission (CSC), Commission on Audit (COA), and Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) statutory requirements.
</p>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Key Metrics at a Glance:</strong><br>
  • <strong>100% Automated Test Pass Rate:</strong> 86 total automated tests executed and passing (31 live API smoke tests + 55 full end-to-end workflow tests).<br>
  • <strong>Zero-Defect TypeScript Builds:</strong> Frontend (<code>vite build</code>) and Backend (<code>tsc</code>) compile with 0 errors.<br>
  • <strong>PostgreSQL Schema Harmonization:</strong> Exactly 10 operational database tables verified in the public schema with full relational constraints.<br>
  • <strong>Host-Reachable Local Runtime:</strong> Network isolation resolved; live backend is directly accessible from desktop Chrome at <code>http://localhost:5173</code>.
</div>

<h2>2. Phase-by-Phase Cumulative Progression</h2>

<table class="data-table">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Phase</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Scope & Objective</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Engineering Deliverables & Actions</th>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Status</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 1</strong></td>
      <td>Repository Audit & Baseline</td>
      <td>Inspected entire stack (Express 5, React 19, TypeScript 5.9, PostgreSQL 18); verified active branch <code>edron-development</code> and commit <code>ce93213</code>; established clean local <code>.env</code> configuration.</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 2</strong></td>
      <td>Database & Backend Validation</td>
      <td>Verified PostgreSQL connectivity on port 5432; executed <code>migration_phase2.sql</code>; built live smoke test suite (<code>live_smoke.ts</code>) passing all 31 security, routing, and CRUD assertions.</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 3</strong></td>
      <td>Frontend / Backend Integration</td>
      <td>Mapped all portal views to Express endpoints; created typed API clients (<code>approvals.ts</code>, <code>audit.ts</code>, <code>disbursement.ts</code>, <code>payroll.ts</code>, <code>users.ts</code>); connected real data across all role views.</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 4</strong></td>
      <td>Implementation Gaps & Password Reset</td>
      <td>Implemented cryptographic password reset endpoints (<code>POST /api/auth/forgot-password</code> and <code>reset-password</code>) using SHA-256 tokens and 1-hour expiry; integrated reset forms in UI.</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 5</strong></td>
      <td>Payroll & Statutory Validation</td>
      <td>Audited compensation formulas: GSIS (9%), PhilHealth (2.5%), Pag-IBIG (₱200 cap), TRAIN tax tables, and PERA (₱2,000 for Permanent/Contractual; ₱0 for Job Order/LWOP); verified 150-byte LandBank batch export.</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 6</strong></td>
      <td>Automated End-to-End Suite</td>
      <td>Authored comprehensive 13-workflow test suite (<code>e2e_workflow_tests.ts</code>) covering positive workflows, negative authorization checks, duplicate detection, and payslip release safeguards.</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 7</strong></td>
      <td>Bug Fixing & Defect Remediation</td>
      <td>Fixed Windows sandbox port isolation; corrected zero-draft computation totals by generating complete <code>PayrollRow</code> entries; aligned Cost Center approval payload keys.</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Phase 8</strong></td>
      <td>Statutory Reports Integration</td>
      <td>Integrated Deduction Reports and official Payroll Register endpoints into API client; expanded automated E2E test coverage to 55 workflows (86 total tests).</td>
      <td><span class="badge-pass">Completed</span></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Database Schema Manifest & Data Integrity</h2>
<p>The system operates against PostgreSQL 18.0. Exactly 10 tables exist within the public schema, fully verified for relational constraints and primary/foreign key cascading:</p>

<table class="data-table">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 5%;">#</th>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Table Name</th>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Verified Rows</th>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Primary Key</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Foreign Keys & Structural Purpose</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>1</td>
      <td><strong>users</strong></td>
      <td>25</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>employee_id -> employees(id)</code>; unique username and email constraints; bcrypt salt-12 hash storage.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>2</td>
      <td><strong>employees</strong></td>
      <td>6</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>employee_no</code> UNIQUE; salary check constraints; employment classifications.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>3</td>
      <td><strong>attendance</strong></td>
      <td>12</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>employee_id -> employees(id)</code> ON DELETE CASCADE; supervisor verification flag and timestamp.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>4</td>
      <td><strong>payroll</strong></td>
      <td>10</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>employee_id -> employees(id)</code>; statutory breakdown JSONB; immutable locking flag.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>5</td>
      <td><strong>approvals</strong></td>
      <td>31</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>payroll_id -> payroll(id)</code> ON DELETE CASCADE; decision history, cost center scoping, remarks.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>6</td>
      <td><strong>approval_routes</strong></td>
      <td>10</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td>Sequence integer, stage names, cost center assignment rules, active flags.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>7</td>
      <td><strong>attachments</strong></td>
      <td>11</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>employee_id -> employees(id)</code> ON DELETE CASCADE; file metadata and disk path storage.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>8</td>
      <td><strong>disbursements</strong></td>
      <td>5</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>payroll_id -> payroll(id)</code> ON DELETE CASCADE; DV number, ORAS/BURAS reference, release status.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>9</td>
      <td><strong>payslips</strong></td>
      <td>5</td>
      <td><code>id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>employee_id</code>, <code>payroll_id</code>; auto-generated employee breakdown upon cashier release.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>10</td>
      <td><strong>audit_logs</strong></td>
      <td>224</td>
      <td><code>log_id</code> (SERIAL)</td>
      <td><code>user_id -> users(id)</code> ON DELETE SET NULL; immutable timestamped event trail.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

